WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.534
ALEX: Fair. What about the Hugging Face
availability — does that change
anything?

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:07.068
ALEX: Because Hugging Face is about as
public as it gets.

00:00:07.178 --> 00:00:10.712
JAMIE: It lowers the friction for
evaluation enormously. A security
researcher who wants

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:14.245
JAMIE: to test this against their actual
incident data doesn't need a procurement

00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:17.779
JAMIE: cycle. They just download it.

00:00:17.889 --> 00:00:19.656
RUFUS: Assuming they have somewhere to
run it that isn't a laptop that

00:00:19.656 --> 00:00:21.423
RUFUS: starts crying.

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:23.998
ALEX: My laptop would do more than cry.

00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:25.027
RUFUS: I wasn't going to say it.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.461
JAMIE: The evaluation piece is genuinely
underrated though. Independent testing
starts the moment

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:33.681
JAMIE: the weights are public. That
forty-seven percent token claim gets
stress-tested faster

00:00:33.681 --> 00:00:37.902
JAMIE: because of Hugging Face, not
slower.
